+//! asset pak) is a separate file on the iPod, read whole into the app's heap
+//! block when the app is picked. The canonical C guest
+//! (engine/guest-quickjs) evaluates it in a QuickJS realm whose malloc is the
+//! same block (programs/nano7g/nanoapps/pocketqjs.c), and the Runtime drives
+//! it through the C guest table, as programs/3ds does.
